(* Content-type: application/vnd.wolfram.mathematica *)
Notebook[{

Cell["Top Quark Signal: Antisymmetric Soft Lines", "Title"],

Cell["A0, A1, A3, A13, AL versus nu = mt/H at fixed r = k12/k34", "Subtitle"],

Cell["Source: Top Quark Signal.pdf, Section 3, Eqs. (78)-(110). This standalone notebook uses ordinary editable Input cells. The independent amplitudes are A0, A1, A3, A13, AL; AP is zero by Eq. (110). The unprojected AP is retained as a numerical diagnostic. The coefficients refer to one cyclic ordering, before Bose symmetrization. No external notebook or package is required.", "Text"],

Cell["1. Conventions and calculation settings", "Section"],

Cell["The default hard-scale ratio is r=1. The f=+ branch is calculated; the other branch is its complex conjugate. The numerical backend evaluates the original time-domain functional (99) with the exact sign kernels (80). This is equivalent to retaining all Hilbert transforms in (95)-(97); it does not truncate the energy-deformation Taylor series. Finite integration bounds and positive Abel damping are explicit numerical controls, not physical parameters. A regulated curve is not a converged zero-damping prediction.", "Text"],

