Cell["6. Quadrature and matrix contraction", "Section"],

Cell["Composite Gauss-Legendre quadrature uses log(z) panels near zero and linear panels at large z. The four-time sum is evaluated as Tr[L K23 R K41], with time and SK labels combined into one matrix index. The weights and ab/cd factors occur once, inside L/R; the cross-edge kernels are inserted before summing branches. Theta(0)=1/2 is used for quadrature diagonals. Mesh refinement checks its finite-grid error.", "Text"],

